<section class="content-card">

<h1>Required Marks Calculator</h1>

<p>
Use this free Required Marks Calculator to find how many marks you
need to achieve your desired percentage in an exam.
</p>

<div class="calc-box">

<label>Desired Percentage (%)</label>
<input id="target" type="number" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="e.g. 80">

<label>Total Marks</label>
<input id="total" type="number" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="e.g. 500">

<button class="calc-btn" onclick="calculateRequired()">
Calculate Required Marks
</button>

<div id="result" class="result"></div>

</div>

</section>

<section class="content-card">

<h2>How to use the Required Marks Calculator</h2>

<ol>
<li>Enter your desired percentage.</li>
<li>Enter the total marks of the exam.</li>
<li>Tap Calculate Required Marks.</li>
<li>The minimum marks required will appear instantly.</li>
</ol>

</section>

<section class="content-card">

<h2>Required marks formula</h2>

<div class="formula">
<strong>Required Marks =</strong>
(Total Marks × Desired Percentage) ÷ 100
</div>

<p>
The result is rounded up to the next whole mark when necessary,
so you know the minimum whole number of marks required.
</p>

</section>

<section class="content-card">

<h2>Example</h2>

<div class="example">
<strong>Desired percentage:</strong> 80%
<br>
<strong>Total marks:</strong> 500
<br><br>
Required Marks = (500 × 80) ÷ 100
<br>
<strong>Required Marks = 400</strong>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content-card">

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

<p>
<strong>How many marks do I need for 80%?</strong><br>
Multiply the total marks by 80 and divide by 100.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Does the calculator round the answer?</strong><br>
Yes. If a fraction of a mark is required, the calculator rounds up
to the next whole mark.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Can I use this for school and university exams?</strong><br>
Yes. It works for any exam where you know the total marks and desired percentage.
</p>

</section>

